{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>And now, let Pharaoh look for a discerning and wise man.</b> He says: there is need for a discerning and wise man to be appointed over the land, and this is ״וישיתהו על ארץ מצרים״ — that is to say, he shall set him supreme over all the people of the land of Egypt. And he said 'discerning' (נבון) — that he know how to manage the people of the land of Egypt with bread according to the children in his hand, and to give them bread sufficient for their survival, and to sell the surplus to other lands to gather money for Pharaoh. And he said 'wise' (חכם) — that he know how to preserve the grain so that it not rot, by mixing it with every kind of substance that preserves it by its nature. And he said thus so that the king would choose him, for the wise man has his eye in his head; thus explained the Ramban, of blessed memory."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:19:24.065097345Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}